/* ============================================================================
   mean-of-data.epher -- arithmetic mean of a dataset, cross-checked as sum/n

   The arithmetic mean (average) of the ten exam scores in `d`, from the
   builtin mean (guide 1.20) and independently as sum(d) / len(d). The two
   must agree, which checks the builtin against the textbook definition.

   Run it from a terminal:  epher "epher scripts/statistics/summary/mean-of-data.epher"
   In the REPL:             load epher scripts/statistics/summary/mean-of-data.epher
   Web/desktop:             paste the whole file into the entry, press Enter
   Everything also works line by line in the TUI.

   The one knob to edit is `d` below. Everything above the results section
   is machinery you can leave alone.
   ============================================================================ */

// ---- the knob -----------------------------------------------------------------
const d = {72, 85, 91, 64, 88, 79, 83, 95, 70, 86}   // exam scores, 10 students, out of 100

// ---- mean by the builtin and by its definition (sum over count) ---------------
mean(d)                     // builtin arithmetic mean
sum(d) / len(d)             // the textbook formula, sum(d) / len(d), agrees

// ---- the pieces of the formula ------------------------------------------------
sum(d)                      // total of all scores
len(d)                      // number of scores

/* ---- expected output ----
= {72, 85, 91, 64, 88, 79, 83, 95, 70, 86}
= 81.3
= 81.3
= 813
= 10
*/